@using Timesheet.Mvc.RazorComponents.Components

<div>Timesheet CRUD Index Page (.cshtml)</div>

<component type="typeof(TimesheetCrud)"
           render-mode="ServerPrerendered" />

<div>
    <h1>Abandoned</h1>

    Razor Components in .NET 8 are designed for Blazor-first apps, not MVC<br />
    The hybrid story is “supported”, but in reality:
    <ul>
        <li>the pipeline order is fragile
        <li>hydration silently fails
        <li>errors hide behind _framework/blazor.server.js
        <li>namespaces matter
        <li>routing order matters
        <li> antiforgery matters
        <li>the hub must be mapped in the right place
        <li>the root component must exist
        <li>the layout must not interfere
        <li>MVC tag helpers can break hydration
    </ul>

    I've spent a day on it. Lets just go straignt to Razor.<br/>
    God help anyone who ever needs to do it this way!
</div>